---
/* The announcement bar, and the first of the three places the accent is spent.
 *
 * docs/DESIGN-SYSTEM.md takes the site's structure from four comparable
 * products that agree almost exactly, and its first line is "thin announcement
 * bar, accent background, one sentence, one link". The site had no such bar at
 * all, which is why the accent had nowhere to land and had drifted onto
 * whatever needed emphasis instead — see the audit in index.astro.
 *
 * WHAT IT SAYS IS A SENTENCE THAT WAS ALREADY ON THE HOME PAGE, moved rather
 * than written. It sat under the hero buttons in 14px grey, where it was the
 * least prominent thing in the hero while being the most important thing a
 * stranger can know about the project. It is now the first line on every page.
 *
 * NO VERSION NUMBER, NO DATE, NO COUNT. A bar reading "v0.9.0 is out" is a
 * claim that decays the moment v0.10.0 ships, on the one element that appears
 * on all 39 pages — and nothing would fail, because a stale banner renders
 * perfectly. Everything here is true for as long as the sentence is true, and
 * changing it is a deliberate edit to this file rather than a release chore
 * somebody forgets.
 *
 * ONE LINK, and it points at the page that says where polyemesis loses. On
 * /comparison itself that is a link to the page you are already on, which is
 * mildly redundant and cheaper than the alternative: a per-page suppression
 * rule is a branch that has to be right on 39 pages to save one reader one
 * pointless click.
 */
---

<div class="announce">
  <p class="wrap flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-x-2 gap-y-0.5">
    <span>Pre-release, one maintainer, MIT.</span>
    <a href="/comparison">Where it loses is written down too&nbsp;→</a>
  </p>
</div>
